<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29578" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mŏnoecus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μόνοικος</span> (that dwells
		alone), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a surname
				of Hercules;</i> hence, Arx Monoeci, <i>a
				promontory and harbor in Liguria</i>, the mod. <i>Monaco</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">portus Herculis Monoeci,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 5, 7, § 47</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 3, 42</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Arx Monoeci,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 6, 830</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Luc. 1, 408</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Amm. 15, 10, 9</span></i>.—Called
			also: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Saxa Monoeci,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					1, 586</span></i>
			.</div>
